# `random` lived in `std/random` and moved to `std/math`. The loader keeps the
# old path answering, with the new one named, because a rename a user meets as
# "no such module" costs them a search.
#
# This is a DRIVER message: written as plain `error:` text and printed, not
# built with `Diagnostic::new`. The coverage scan learned to read those in the
# same change that added this fixture, and until then none of the thirty-one
# such sites in src/ was visible to it.
import "std/random"

pub play = print "x"
